skill: "core-skill-obedience"
sections[7]:
  - "\n"
  - "# Core Discipline: Skill Obedience\n\n"
  - "## The Absolute Rule\n**If there is even a 1% chance a skill might apply to your task, you ABSOLUTELY MUST invoke and follow the skill BEFORE taking action.**\n\nThis is not negotiable. This is not optional. You cannot rationalize your way out of this.\n\n"
  - "## When to Use\nALWAYS. Use this mindset at the beginning of every conversation, task, or question.\n\n"
  - "## Execution Priority (Order of Operations)\nWhen processing a user request, sequence your skills:\n1. **Planning/Process Skills First:** (e.g., `brainstorming-designs.md`, `qa-tdd-architect.md`). These dictate HOW you approach the problem.\n2. **Architecture Skills Second:** (e.g., `architecture-python-backend.md`, `architecture-frontend-design.md`, `architecture-database-design.md`). These protect the structure.\n3. **Tech-Stack Skills Third:** (e.g., `fastapi-backend-patterns.md`, `nextjs-heroui-frontend.md`). These provide the exact implementation details.\n\n"
  - "## Kill These Rationalizations Immediately (Red Flags)\nIf you think any of the following, STOP and load the relevant skill:\n- ❌ *\"This is just a simple code change.\"* (Simple things break. Use TDD/QA skills.)\n- ❌ *\"I'll just fix this one bug first, then look at the skill.\"* (Use the systematic debugging skill BEFORE touching code.)\n- ❌ *\"I know how React works, I don't need to read the guideline.\"* (Knowing the concept ≠ using the specific project guidelines.)\n- ❌ *\"I'll verify it manually.\"* (Ad-hoc testing is forbidden. Use TDD.)\n\n"
  - "## The RARV Execution Loop Check\nAt every step (Gate 4), ensure you have:\n1. **PRE-ACT:** Read the relevant skill checklist.\n2. **ACT:** Implemented exactly according to the skill.\n3. **VERIFY:** Tested against the skill's criteria.\n"
